+// Wave3 DX (determinism-audit/fixes): strict-mode
+// determinism fixes on top of exactness mode (overlay-xm). Every fix is off unless
+// its environment knob (or the GUFO_DX master switch) turns it on; with nothing
+// set the overlay runs overlay-xm's statements (= production for strict requests).
+//
+//   GUFO_DX=1                    master: F0 + G2 + F3 + SPARSE_BY_POSITION +
+//                                TOOL_IDS + CHUNK=2048 (ROWINV stays off).
+//                                Each knob below overrides the master ("0"/"1").
+//   R3-22 / F0  GUFO_DX_F0       fixed component-cache budget (GUFO_DX_CACHE_BYTES,
+//                                default 9e9 = T1's pin) instead of HostAvailable/2, and a
+//                                backing pool of GUFO_DX_BACKING_BYTES (default
+//                                2.125 GiB, production's load-time pool) committed
+//                                completely at load and never grown afterwards (no
+//                                device-heap- or 1 s-timer-gated growth).
+//                                GUFO_DX_F0_SHORT=fail|clamp: a pool that cannot be
+//                                committed at load fails the load (default) or is
+//                                kept and logged deterministic=0.
+//   G2          GUFO_DX_G2       commit-aware clamp: a backing segment is admitted
+//                                only if Windows commit headroom stays above
+//                                GUFO_DX_COMMIT_RESERVE_GIB (default 8) after it.
+//   F3          GUFO_DX_F3       transfer fences: cache captures wait (GPU event) for
+//                                the executor stream, borrowed rows and P9 snapshot
+//                                protection synchronize it on the host first.
+//   R3-20       GUFO_DX_SPARSE_BY_POSITION
+//                                narrow attention takes the dense key sweep for
+//                                every row below indexer_top_k, also in a chain that
+//                                crosses it (production: chain-wide sparse flag).
+//   R3-21       GUFO_DX_ROWINV   prototype: decode batches wider than 8 rows run the
+//                                dense projections and the MoE in <= 8-row solo
+//                                launches and the GDN per session, so a row's bits
+//                                equal its solo decode (diagnostic; costs C8 speed).
+//   R3-23       GUFO_DX_CHUNK=N  prefill budget = a pure function of the prompt:
+//                                cuts every N tokens (multiple of 128, 256..8192)
+//                                from the restore point (GUFO_DX_CHUNK_GRID=relative,
+//                                default) or from position 0 (absolute); a tail of
+//                                <= 128 rows joins the last chunk. 0 = production.
